# Impractical Joke: "Damage can't be prevented this turn" (CR 615.12), cast with no target at all, so the damage it does
# is none and only the rider matters. On turn 5 Bot1's Embereth Shieldbreaker (red, 2/1) attacks and Bot2's Ornithopter
# (0/2) blocks it; Bot2's Giver of Runes gives the Ornithopter protection from red, whose damage prevention (CR 702.16e)
# is itself prevented from happening: the Shieldbreaker's 2 damage is dealt and the Ornithopter dies. The same combat
# without the Joke is impractical-joke-not-cast-protection-from-red-prevents-the-damage, where the Ornithopter survives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Impractical Joke
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Giver of Runes
Ornithopter
Plains x4
Plains x12

